{"slug": "tahini-ramen-salad", "nyt_id": 1024037, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1024037-tahini-ramen-salad", "name": "Tahini Ramen Salad", "author": "Kay Chun", "description": "A breeze to make on busy weeknights, this fresh, colorful ramen salad is equally tasty at room temperature or chilled — which means it’s particularly picnic-friendly. Chickpeas add creamy texture, contrasting the crisp bite of vibrant veggies. Use your favorite combination: Yellow bell peppers, cucumbers, snap peas, radishes, celery, asparagus and cabbage are all great options. You can make the salad an hour ahead and let the savory tahini-garlic sauce soak into the noodles (at room temperature); just give it a quick toss before serving so that everything is evenly coated in the luscious sauce. If chilled, pull the salad from the refrigerator 10 minutes before serving to allow the sauce to soften, then give it a nice mix.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 20, "cook_minutes": 10, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"prep": "PT20M", "cook": "PT10M", "total": "PT30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "12 ounces dry ramen noodles (or four 3-ounce individual packages, seasoning packets discarded or reserved for another use)", "group": null, "quantity": 12.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "dry ramen noodles (or four 3-ounce individual packages", "preparation": "seasoning packets discarded or reserved for another use)", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "6 tablespoons tahini", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "tahini", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "6 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "¼ cup distilled white vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "distilled white vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 tablespoons minced ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 tablespoons sweet miso", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sweet miso", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 tablespoon minced garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Kosher salt and black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "kosher salt and black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 (15-ounce) can chickpeas, rinsed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "can", "item": "chickpeas", "preparation": "rinsed", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "4 cups thinly sliced vegetables (such as yellow bell pepper, cucumbers, radishes and snap peas)", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "thinly sliced vegetables (such as yellow bell pepper", "preparation": "cucumbers, radishes and snap peas)", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ cup thinly sliced scallions", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "thinly sliced scallions", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a medium pot of boiling water, cook the ramen noodles according to package directions until al dente. Drain, rinse under cold water until cool, then drain well; transfer to a large bowl."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a small bowl, combine tahini, oil, vinegar, ginger, miso, garlic and ¼ cup of water. Season with salt and pepper and whisk until smooth."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Add ½ cup of the dressing to the noodles, season and toss to coat. Add chickpeas, sliced vegetables, scallions and remaining dressing; season and toss to coat. Serve at room temperature or chilled."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 932.0, "protein_g": 24.6, "carbohydrates_g": 97.3, "fat_g": 51.3, "saturated_fat_g": 11.8, "unsaturated_fat_g": 10.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 2232.8, "fiber_g": 16.2, "sugar_g": 7.0, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-lunch-main-course-noodles-salad-side-dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["chickpea", "easy", "picnic", "quick", "ramen-noodle", "spring", "summer", "tahini", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/04/13/multimedia/kc-tahini-ramen-salad-qflh/kc-tahini-ramen-salad-qflh-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/04/13/multimedia/kc-tahini-ramen-salad-qflh/kc-tahini-ramen-salad-qflh-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/04/13/multimedia/kc-tahini-ramen-salad-qflh/kc-tahini-ramen-salad-qflh-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/04/13/multimedia/kc-tahini-ramen-salad-qflh/kc-tahini-ramen-salad-qflh-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 962}, "video_url": "https://vp.nyt.com/video/2024/06/18/119796_1_Tahini-Ramen-Salad-Vertical-Video_wg_480p.mp4", "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2023-04-13", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:27:43Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "tandoori-mushrooms", "nyt_id": 1013600, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013600-tandoori-mushrooms", "name": "Tandoori Mushrooms", "author": "Steven Raichlen", "description": "Steven Raichlen", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "PT30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 2-inch piece peeled ginger, roughly chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "inch piece peeled ginger", "preparation": "roughly chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 cloves garlic, peeled and roughly chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "peeled and roughly chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 teaspoon salt, more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": "more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 teaspoon ground cumin", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cumin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 teaspoon red chili powder or hot paprika", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "red chili powder or hot paprika", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ teaspoon ground turmeric", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground turmeric", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ teaspoon white pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "white pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "¼ cup fresh lemon juice (from 2 lemons)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 tablespoons vegetable oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "vegetable oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "¾ cup sour cream", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "unit": "cup", "item": "sour cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "3 tablespoons plain Greek yogurt", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "plain greek yogurt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "12 ounces cremini, portobello or other mushrooms, trimmed", "group": null, "quantity": 12.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "cremini", "preparation": "portobello or other mushrooms, trimmed", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place the ginger, garlic, salt, cumin, chili powder, turmeric and white pepper in a food processor. Finely chop, scraping down the sides of the bowl with a rubber spatula. Add the lemon juice and 1 tablespoon vegetable oil, and purée. Add the sour cream and yogurt, and pulse processor in short bursts, just to mix. Transfer marinade to a glass, ceramic or stainless steel mixing bowl."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Wipe mushrooms clean with damp paper towels. Stir mushrooms into the marinade. Cover and refrigerate for 30 minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "If using a tandoor, heat it to 500 degrees. If using a grill or broiler, heat to high."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Thread mushrooms on bamboo or metal skewers. In tandoor, cook mushrooms until lightly browned on outside, 2 to 3 minutes. Baste with 1 tablespoon oil and continue cooking until golden brown and tender, 1 to 2 minutes more. If grilling or broiling, cook mushrooms until golden and tender, 3 to 4 minutes a side, 6 to 8 minutes total, basting with oil."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 192.0, "protein_g": 4.6, "carbohydrates_g": 9.3, "fat_g": 16.5, "saturated_fat_g": 5.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 1.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.4, "cholesterol_mg": 27.2, "sodium_mg": 397.8, "fiber_g": 1.1, "sugar_g": 3.9, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["indian"], "diet": [], "course": ["side-dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["cremini", "easy", "portobello", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/03/dining/tandoori-mushrooms/tandoori-mushrooms-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/03/dining/tandoori-mushrooms/tandoori-mushrooms-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 64}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2011-05-11", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:45:05Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "tangy-red-lentil-soup-with-nicoise-olives", "nyt_id": 1012411, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1012411-tangy-red-lentil-soup-with-nicoise-olives", "name": "Tangy Red Lentil Soup With Niçoise Olives", "author": "Jane Sigal", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "8 servings", "min": 8, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 45, "raw": {"total": "PT45M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 large celery stalk, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large celery stalk", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 large carrot, unpeeled, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large carrot", "preparation": "unpeeled, finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 large onion, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large onion", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "3 garlic cloves, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "¼ cup extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 tablespoons tomato paste", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "tomato paste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 pound red lentils, rinsed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "lb", "item": "red lentils", "preparation": "rinsed", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 pound chicken backs", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "lb", "item": "chicken backs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "4 thyme sprigs", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "thyme sprigs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 lemons, halved", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "lemons", "preparation": "halved", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "¼ cup whole niçoise olives", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "whole niçoise olives", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a 4-quart saucepan, combine celery, carrot, onion, garlic, olive oil and salt. Cover and cook over low heat, stirring occasionally, until soft, about 10 minutes. Stir in tomato paste and cook 1 minute. Add lentils, chicken backs, 8 cups water and thyme, and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to medium-low and simmer, uncovered, until lentils have broken down, about 30 minutes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Discard thyme sprigs. Remove chicken backs, remove meat from bones, chop meat and return meat to soup. Using an immersion blender, partially purée soup. Taste and add salt if needed. Ladle soup into bowls, squeeze in lemon juice and serve topped with olives."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 469.75, "protein_g": 22.8, "carbohydrates_g": 42.5, "fat_g": 24.2, "saturated_fat_g": 5.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 4.6, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 44.8, "sodium_mg": 436.5, "fiber_g": 7.8, "sugar_g": 3.5, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mediterranean"], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course-soup"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["chicken", "great-leftovers", "red-lentil"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 18}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2009-02-25", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:30:10Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "tapa-of-mushrooms-in-garlic-sauce", "nyt_id": 1013385, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013385-tapa-of-mushrooms-in-garlic-sauce", "name": "Tapa of Mushrooms in Garlic Sauce", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "You find these mushrooms served in little ceramic casseroles at tapas bars all over Spain. It’s a simple hors d’oeuvre that can be made ahead and reheated. In Spain, it would be made with about four times as much olive oil and served in small ceramic cazuelas. You also can serve the mushrooms with toothpicks.", "servings": {"text": "8 as part of an assortment of tapas", "min": 8, "max": 8, "yield_type": "other"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "PT20M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "4 garlic cloves, thinly sliced or minced", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "thinly sliced or minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 small dried red chili, crumbled, or ¼ to ½ teaspoon red pepper flakes", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "small dried red chili", "preparation": "crumbled, or ¼ to ½ teaspoon red pepper flakes", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 pounds mushrooms, wiped clean, stems trimmed, cut in half", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "lb", "item": "mushrooms", "preparation": "wiped clean, stems trimmed, cut in half", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ cup dry white wine or fino sherry", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry white wine or fino sherry", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 tablespoon fresh lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped fresh parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "{'@type': 'HowToStep', 'text': 'Heat the oil over medium heat in a large, heavy nonstick skillet. Add the garlic and chili or red pepper flakes. After about 30 seconds, when the garlic begins to sizzle, add the mushrooms and turn the heat to medium high. Cook, stirring, until they sear and begin to sweat, then sprinkle them with salt and add the white wine or sherry. Turn the heat down to medium, and continue to cook, stirring or tossing in the pan from time to time, until the mushrooms are tender, five to 10 minutes. Stir in the lemon juice and parsley, taste and adjust seasonings, and remove from the heat. Serve hot or warm in small ceramic dishes, or serve on a platter with toothpicks stuck into the mushrooms.', 'url': 'https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013385-tapa-of-mushrooms-in-garlic-sauce#recipe-step-1'}"}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 67.75, "protein_g": 3.7, "carbohydrates_g": 5.2, "fat_g": 3.8, "saturated_fat_g": 0.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.5, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 296.8, "fiber_g": 1.2, "sugar_g": 2.4, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["spanish"], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["easy", "garlic", "mushroom", "quick"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2010/12/14/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2010/12/14/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "